          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represented
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            is also called
            = succeed "," do
              %em stable cohomotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            version of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomotopy"} cohomotopy
          %p
            Equivalently, it is the cohomological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            concept to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+homology+theory"} stable homotopy homology theory
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+theorem"} Pontryagin-Thom theorem
            this is equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} framed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AsAlgebraicKTheoryOverTheFieldWithOneElement
            As algebraic K-theory over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
          %p
            The following is known as the
            = succeed ":" do
              %em Barratt-Priddy-Quillen theorem
          #StableCohomotopyIsKTheoryOfFinSet.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+cohomotopy"} stable cohomotopy
                is K-theory of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} =
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
              of the category of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+category"} permutative category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+permutative+category"} K-theory of this permutative category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K(FinSet) \;\simeq\; \mathbb{S}
            %p
              is represented by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
          %p
            This is due to
            %a{:href => "#BarrattPriddy72"} Barratt-Priddy 72
            reproved in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Segal74"} Segal 74, Prop. 3.5
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Priddy73"} Priddy 73
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Glasman13"} Glasman 13
          #StableCohomotopyIsAlgebraicKTheoryOverFieldWithOneElement.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+cohomotopy"} stable cohomotopy
                as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
                over the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"} field with one element
            %p
              Notice that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+permutative+category"} K-theory of a permutative category
              of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F Mod
              is its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K F
              (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "K-theory+of+a+permutative+category#OrdinaryAlgebraicKTheoryFromPermutativeCategoryOfProjectiveModules"} this example
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K F \;\simeq\; K(F Mod)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"}> pointed
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
              may be regarded as the modules over the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"}> field with one element
              ”
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
              (see
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "field+with+one+element#Modules"} there
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 1
                    %mi Mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{F}_1 Mod
                    \\;=\;
                    FinSet^{\ast/}
            %p
              If this is understood, example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableCohomotopyIsKTheoryOfFinSet"}
              says that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+cohomotopy"} stable cohomotopy
              is the algebraic K-theory of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"} field with one element
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S} \;\simeq\; K \mathbb{F}_1
                    \\,.
          %p
            This perspective is highlighted in:
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Deitmar06"} Deitmar 06, p. 2
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Guillot06"} Guillot 06
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Mahanta17"} Mahanta 17
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#DundasGoodwillieMcCarthy13"} Dundas, Goodwillie* McCarthy 13, II 1.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MoravaSomeBackground"} Morava
            %a{:href => "#ConnesConsani16"} Connes &amp; Consani 16
            and fully explicitly in
            %a{:href => "#ChuLorscheidSanthanam10"} Chu, Lorscheid &amp; Santhanam 10, Thm. 5.9
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BeardsleyNakamura24"} Beardsley &amp; Nakamura 2024, Cor. 2.25
            %a{:href => "#ChuLorscheidSanthanam10"} Chu et al.
            also generalize to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+Cohomotopy"} equivariant stable Cohomotopy
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"}> equivariant
                    )
