                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+mO"}> global equivariant mO
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+mU"} global equivariant mU
            %p algebraic:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+cobordism"} algebraic cobordism
          %h2#references References
          %p The concept of stable Cohomotopy as such:
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                , part III, section 6, p. 204 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Rognes"}> John Rognes
                , p. 1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The sphere spectrum
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/RognesSphereSpectrum.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of stable Cohomotopy as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} framed
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
          %ul
            %li#Stong68
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Stong"}> Robert Stong
              , Chapter IV, Example 1, p. 40 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on Cobordism theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://pi.math.virginia.edu/StongConf/Stongbookcontents.pdf"} toc pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://press.princeton.edu/titles/6465.html"} ISBN:9780691649016
          %p
            Discussion of stable Cohomotopy of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                C. T. Stretch,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stable cohomotopy and cobordism of abelian groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100058734"} doi:10.1017/S0305004100058734
            %li
              %p
                Ken-ichi Maruyama,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi e
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                    \-invariants on the stable cohomotopy groups of Lie groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ojm/1200780982"} euclid:ojm/1200780982
            %li
              %p
                Sławomir Nowak,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stable cohomotopy groups of compact spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.impan.pl/en/publishing-house/journals-and-series/fundamenta-mathematicae/all/180/2"} doi:10.4064/fm180-2-1
          %p
            The identification of stable cohomotopy with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+permutative+category"} K-theory of the permutative category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#BarrattPriddy72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barratt"}> Michael Barratt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stewart+Priddy"} Stewart Priddy
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the homology of non-connected monoids and their associated groups
                %strong 47
                1 (1972) 1–14 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF02566785"}> doi:10.1007/BF02566785
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/139496"} eudml:139496
            %li#Segal74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories and cohomology theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(74)90022-6"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(74)90022-6
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SegalCategoriesAndCohomologyTheories.pdf"} pdf
          %p see also:
          %ul
            %li#Priddy73
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stewart+Priddy"}> Stewart Priddy
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Transfer, symmetric groups, and stable homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher K-Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/BFb0067060.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Glasman13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+Glasman"}> Saul Glasman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The multiplicative Barratt-Priddy-Quillen theorem and beyond
                %em AMS Sectional Meeting
                %strong 1095
                (2013) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/meetings/sectional/2199_program_ss7.html"}> webpage
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~sglasman/bpq-beamer.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pedro+Boavida+de+Brito"}> Pedro Boavida de Brito
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Dendroidal spaces,
                    = succeed "-spaces" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Γ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                %strong 2020
                760 (2020) 229-265 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.06459"}> arXiv:1701.06459
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/crelle-2018-0002"} doi:10.1515/crelle-2018-0002
          %p
            The resulting interpretation of stable cohomotopy as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"} field with one element
            is amplified in the following texts:
          %ul
            %li#DundasGoodwillieMcCarthy13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bj%C3%B8rn+Dundas"}> Bjørn Dundas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Goodwillie"} Thomas Goodwillie
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Randy+McCarthy"} Randy McCarthy
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The local structure of algebraic K-theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4471-4393-2"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4471-4393-2
            %li#Deitmar06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Deitmar"}> Anton Deitmar
                ,
                %em
                  Remarks on zeta functions and K-theory over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0605429"}> arXiv:math/0605429
                )
            %li#Guillot06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Guillot"}> Pierre Guillot
                ,
                %em Adams operations in cohomotopy
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0612327"}> arXiv:0612327
                )
            %li#Mahanta17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snigdhayan+Mahanta"}> Snigdhayan Mahanta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    G-theory of
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔽
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.6001"} arXiv:1110.6001
            %li#ChuLorscheidSanthanam10
              %p
                Chenghao Chu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oliver+Lorscheid"} Oliver Lorscheid
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Sheaves and K-theory for
                    = succeed "-schemes" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔽
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
                %strong 229
                4, (2012) 2239-2286 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1010.2896"}> arxiv:1010.2896
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2011.12.023"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2011.12.023
            %li#BeardsleyNakamura24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Beardsley"}> Jonathan Beardsley
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/So+Nakamura"} So Nakamura
                %em
                  Projective Geometries and Simple Pointed Matroids as
                  = succeed "-modules" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔽
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.04730"}> arXiv:2404.04730
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p see also
          %ul
            %li#MoravaSomeBackground
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jack+Morava"}> Jack Morava
                ,
                %em
                  Some background on Manin’s theorem
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi 𝕊
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{F}_1) \sim \mathbb{S}
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.alainconnes.org/docs/Morava.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MoravaSomeBackground.pdf", :title => ""} MoravaSomeBackground.pdf
            %li#ConnesConsani16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Caterina+Consani"} Caterina Consani
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Absolute algebra and Segal’s Gamma sets
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.05585"} arXiv:1502.05585
            %li#Berman18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+D.+Berman"}> John D. Berman
                , p. 92 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorified algebra and equivariant homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08745"} arXiv:1805.08745
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.people.virginia.edu/~jdb8pc/Thesis.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kahn-Priddy+theorem"} Kahn-Priddy theorem
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#KahnPriddy72
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kahn"}> Daniel Kahn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stewart+Priddy"} Stewart Priddy
              = succeed "," do
                %em Applications of the transfer to stable homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.bams/1183534135"} Euclid
          %p
            Discussion of stable Cohomotopy as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} framed
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
          %ul
            %li#ConnerFloyd66
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Conner"}> Pierre Conner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Floyd"} Edwin Floyd
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Relation+of+Cobordism+to+K-Theories"} The Relation of Cobordism to K-Theories
              %strong 28
              Springer 1966 (
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0071091"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0071091
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=216511"} MR216511
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CE%B2-rings"} β-rings
            is discussed in
          %ul
